Study programme objectives.text:
To provide knowledge of the safe operation of the ship in cargo and passenger transportation, watch procedures on deck and bridge;
To teach how monitor the manoeuvring of the ship; plan cargo operations and monitor their progress;
To provide knowledge of international conventions and other international and national normative acts;
To teach how to monitor the compliance of the ship's operation with legislative requirements relating to safety of life at sea, security and protection of the marine environment;
To provide an understanding of the technical supervision, maintenance and repair of the ship; delivery of the necessary materials and supplies on board, compliance of the ship's crew and other employees with the performance of their assigned duties, maintenance of records of the performed activities;
To teach how to ensure the transmission and reception of routine and emergency information by means of radio communications with other ships and shore stations;
To teach leadership and management tasks including conflict resolution, teamwork, project management and other elements of management to contribute to the development of students' management skills.
To strengthen students' foreign language skills to facilitate effective communication in an international maritime environment.

- To provide knowledge of the theoretical basis and operating, planning and management principles of engineering, electrical, electronic and control systems on board ships;
- To provide knowledge and proficiency of the operation, planning and management of operation, maintenance and repair of ships' main propulsion and auxiliary machinery;
- To provide knowledge and proficiency of the operation, planning and management of operation, maintenance and repair of ships' electrical, electronic and control systems;
- To teach how to solve engineering, electrical and electronic control, maintenance and repair tasks on board ships, based on practical and theoretical knowledge;
- To teach how to deal with situations related to safety management, emergency prevention and response, and environmental policy and practice, providing students with the necessary knowledge and skills;
- To teach leadership and management skills including conflict resolution, teamwork, project management and other elements of management to contribute to the development of students' management skills;
- Provide knowledge of relevant international maritime norms and standards, including IMO standards, to ensure students' understanding of international regulations and requirements;
- To strengthen students' foreign language skills to facilitate effective communication in an international maritime environment.
